{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "cartesian_rings_regrid_3x3_to_2x2",
    "description": "HEADLINE conformance fixture: the conservative-regridding story END-TO-END DECLARATIVE -- grid spec -> cell rings -> narrow phase -> assembly -> apply, with NO out-of-document precomputation. The consumer supplies only the target GRID SPEC (origin tgt_x0/tgt_y0 = 0, spacing tgt_dx/tgt_dy = 1.5, sizes GX = GY = 2 bound at the regridding/cartesian_cell_rings.esm import edge) and the source data; the geometry is derived in-library: tgt_poly and the centers tgt_lon/tgt_lat come from the cartesian_cell_rings_{poly,lon,lat} affine templates over the flattened row-major cell enumeration (cell c = (y-1)*GX + x, southwest origin -- exactly the dense exemplar's target enumeration), and the constructed rings flow straight into the conservative_overlap narrow phase / assembly / apply at manifold 'planar'. The DENSE narrow phase here is the ungated companion to the CANDIDATE-GATED sibling cartesian_rings_regrid_gated_3x3_to_2x2, which feeds the SAME constructed rings and the SAME constructed centers (tgt_lon/tgt_lat) through the bin-Skolem broad phase end-to-end: the EarthSciAST.jl tree-walk restriction that once barred a template-CONSTRUCTED (aggregate-valued) coordinate buffer from being a value-invention skolem index target (E_TREEWALK_VI_INDEX) has been lifted, so the constructed centers now flow straight into the bin keys. The two cases are value-identical (the gated sibling asserts gated == dense at abs 0.0) and share this golden, so the dense spelling stays the readable narrow-phase reference while the sibling exercises the gated path. AFFINE-FORMULA GATE (the archived verify script's check, promoted to a conformance assertion): affine_state integrates sum|tgt_poly - tgt_poly_expected| + sum|tgt_lon - tgt_lon_expected| + sum|tgt_lat - tgt_lat_expected| against inline expected constants and is asserted EXACTLY ZERO (abs 0.0) -- x0 + (x-1)*dx and its corner offsets are sums/products of exactly-representable doubles here (0, 1.5, 3.0, 0.75, 2.25), so the template output is bit-exact against the hand geometry. The GEOMETRY IS THE DENSE EXEMPLAR'S: the constructed 2x2 target over [0,3]^2 equals conservative_overlap_3x3_to_2x2's hand-authored tgt_poly ring for ring, so the golden per-pair weights (official Julia runner, scripts/regenerate-goldens.sh) must reproduce the same exact rationals (A_ij corner 1.0 / edge 0.5 / center 0.25, A_j = 2.25, W = 4/9 / 2/9 / 1/9, F_tgt = [7/3, 11/3, 19/3, 23/3]) -- constructed and hand-authored geometry are interchangeable inputs to the same regridder. The 5.8.3 EXACT invariants (partition-of-unity by construction, conservation because the constructed target tiles the source domain) gate the pipeline; src rings stay consumer data here (a 3x3 unit-cell tiling) because one document supports ONE cartesian_cell_rings import (the ring_* index sets are metaparameter-sized, esm-spec 9.7.5/9.7.6).",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "regridding",
      "cartesian_cell_rings",
      "conservative_overlap",
      "end-to-end",
      "declarative-geometry",
      "affine",
      "template-import",
      "partition-of-unity",
      "conservation"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Regrid": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../../../../regridding/conservative_overlap.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NSRC": 9,
            "NTGT": 4,
            "NVERT": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../../regridding/cartesian_cell_rings.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "GX": 2,
            "GY": 2
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "atol": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1e-12,
          "description": "Sliver floor (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.2), as in the dense exemplar."
        },
        "tgt_x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "TARGET GRID SPEC: west-most cell-edge x-coordinate (the affine origin of the x axis)."
        },
        "tgt_y0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "TARGET GRID SPEC: south-most cell-edge y-coordinate."
        },
        "tgt_dx": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 1.5,
          "description": "TARGET GRID SPEC: uniform x spacing. With GX = 2 the constructed grid tiles [0,3] exactly."
        },
        "tgt_dy": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 1.5,
          "description": "TARGET GRID SPEC: uniform y spacing."
        },
        "src_poly": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells",
            "overlap_cell_verts",
            "overlap_coord"
          ],
          "description": "Source-cell geometry (consumer data): nine closed CCW rings, 1x1-degree cells tiling [0,3]^2, row-major from the southwest -- the dense exemplar's source grid."
        },
        "tgt_poly": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells",
            "overlap_cell_verts",
            "overlap_coord"
          ],
          "description": "CONSTRUCTED target-cell geometry: the four-corner CCW rings emitted by cartesian_cell_rings_poly from the grid spec alone (flattened row-major over ring_cells = GX*GY = 4 = NTGT). Expected bit-equal to the dense exemplar's hand-authored rings (tgt_poly_expected; the affine_formula gate)."
        },
        "tgt_lon": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "deg",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "CONSTRUCTED target centers (x): cartesian_cell_rings_lon from the grid spec. Expected [0.75, 2.25, 0.75, 2.25] (the affine_formula gate pins them exactly); these are the coordinates a broad-phase consumer would bin on."
        },
        "tgt_lat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "deg",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "CONSTRUCTED target centers (y). Expected [0.75, 0.75, 2.25, 2.25]."
        },
        "tgt_poly_expected": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells",
            "overlap_cell_verts",
            "overlap_coord"
          ],
          "description": "AFFINE-FORMULA ORACLE: the hand-authored rings of the dense exemplar (row-major from the southwest, CCW (W,S)->(E,S)->(E,N)->(W,N)). Every coordinate (0, 1.5, 3.0) is exactly representable, so the constructor must match bit-for-bit."
        },
        "tgt_lon_expected": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "deg",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "AFFINE-FORMULA ORACLE: hand centers x (0.75 and 2.25 exactly representable)."
        },
        "tgt_lat_expected": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "deg",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "AFFINE-FORMULA ORACLE: hand centers y."
        },
        "ring_err": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "L1 residual of the constructed rings against the affine oracle: sum_{c,v,k} |tgt_poly - tgt_poly_expected|. Exactly 0.0."
        },
        "center_err": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "L1 residual of the constructed centers against the affine oracle: sum_c |tgt_lon - tgt_lon_expected| + |tgt_lat - tgt_lat_expected|. Exactly 0.0."
        },
        "src_area": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "True source-cell areas (1 deg^2 each) for the conservation invariant."
        },
        "F_src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "The source field, F[i] = i (the exemplar field; F_tgt = [7/3, 11/3, 19/3, 23/3], mass 45)."
        },
        "unit_src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "The constant-1 source field for the partition-of-unity surface."
        },
        "A_ij": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells",
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "DENSE narrow phase on the CONSTRUCTED target rings, manifold 'planar' (esm-spec 8.6.1's blessed dense spelling; the candidate-gated variant on this same constructed geometry is the sibling case cartesian_rings_regrid_gated_3x3_to_2x2, gated == dense at abs 0.0). Expected the exemplar's exact areas: corner 1.0, edge 0.5, center 0.25 deg^2."
        },
        "A_j": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Row normalization (the denominator is the row-sum of the SAME computed areas under the SAME sliver filter, so partition-of-unity is exact by construction). Expected 2.25 for every j."
        },
        "W_ij": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells",
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Normalized weights (same filter as A_j/apply). Expected the exemplar's exact rationals 4/9, 2/9, 1/9."
        },
        "F_tgt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "The regridded field through the library apply. Expected [7/3, 11/3, 19/3, 23/3]."
        },
        "F_unit_tgt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "The constant-1 field through the same apply: partition-of-unity as an ordinary field, exactly 1 by construction."
        },
        "mass_src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Source-side mass sum_i A_i*F_src[i] = 45."
        },
        "mass_tgt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Target-side mass sum_j A_j*F_tgt[j] with the computed denominators as target areas. Equals mass_src exactly (the CONSTRUCTED target tiles the source domain)."
        },
        "pou_state": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Surfacing state for partition-of-unity: pou_state(1) = sum_i W_ij."
        },
        "cons_state": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Surfacing state for the conservation residual: cons_state(1) = mass_tgt - mass_src = 0."
        },
        "regrid_state": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Surfacing state for the regridded field: regrid_state(1) = F_tgt."
        },
        "affine_state": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Surfacing state for the AFFINE-FORMULA gate: affine_state(1) = ring_err + center_err, the total L1 residual of the constructed geometry against the inline oracle -- asserted EXACTLY zero (abs 0.0), the archived verify script's 0.0-error check as a conformance assertion."
        }
      },
